.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_VERIFY_EX 3 2026-11-16 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_verify_ex \- compare stored archive metadata and report coverage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_verify_ex("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "verify_flags,"
.BI "        uint32_t *" "checked,"
.BI "        uint32_t *" "unavailable,"
.BI "        uint32_t *" "mismatches"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute fresh MD5 comparisons of serialized MPQ metadata against the opened
archive's validated reference descriptors. This operation is distinct from
.BR libmpq__archive_verify (3),
which verifies digital signatures using a public key, and
.BR libmpq__file_verify_ex (3),
which verifies individual members. The _ex suffix does not imply that these
archive functions verify the same integrity domain.
.PP
Combine any of LIBMPQ_VERIFY_METADATA_HEADER_MD5, LIBMPQ_VERIFY_METADATA_HASH_MD5,
LIBMPQ_VERIFY_METADATA_BLOCK_MD5, LIBMPQ_VERIFY_METADATA_HI_BLOCK_MD5,
LIBMPQ_VERIFY_METADATA_HET_MD5, LIBMPQ_VERIFY_METADATA_BET_MD5,
LIBMPQ_VERIFY_METADATA_HET_RAW_MD5 and LIBMPQ_VERIFY_METADATA_BET_RAW_MD5.
LIBMPQ_VERIFY_METADATA_ALL requests all eight. Other bits, including member
verification flags and signature selectors, are rejected. Zero flags perform
no integrity comparison after handle and output validation.
.PP
The six structural checks hash original stored bytes, including encrypted or
compressed table representations. Each supplied expected digest is compared
with the opened reference and with the digest of the stored object. Changes
to stored reference fields are mismatches, including zeroing a previously
present field. Changed header geometry is never adopted. Present empty tables
with supplied references compare MD5 of the empty sequence.
.PP
Older versions, absent optional tables and all-zero structural reference fields
are unavailable. HET/BET trailing RAW arrays are unavailable for older versions,
absent tables or zero raw chunk size. With nonzero v4 raw chunk size, present
nonempty HET/BET tables require complete trailing arrays. Missing, truncated,
overlapping or arithmetically invalid required storage is an operational error;
readable zero-filled or arbitrary checksum bytes are actually compared.
.SS Results
On success checked and unavailable partition the requested mask, and mismatches
is a subset of checked. The two coverage masks never overlap. A checksum
mismatch returns success with its bit set, not an operational error.
Complete matching requested coverage requires:
.nf
    status == 0
    checked == verify_flags
    unavailable == 0
    mismatches == 0
.fi
.PP
All three outputs are required. Any operational failure clears all non-NULL
outputs, including results of earlier comparisons in the same call.
.SS Source and scope
Reads use the existing source abstraction and original MPQ-relative descriptors,
with the handle's own embedded origin or MPQE logical decoding. Prefix bytes
are not header/table input. The backing source must remain stable. This is
neither an atomic snapshot under concurrent writes nor an uncached filesystem
audit. Reopen a stable source to adopt changed archive geometry.
.PP
Matching unkeyed MD5 values do not establish authenticity or provenance.
This operation does not verify every member, listfile completeness, semantic
attributes, signatures, arbitrary container prefixes or MPQE transport
authenticity. Existing reader structures and mappings remain unchanged.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
/* archive is an open reader. A missing digest cannot produce a match. */
int32_t
check_header_md5(mpq_archive_s *archive, int *matched)
{
    const uint32_t requested = LIBMPQ_VERIFY_METADATA_HEADER_MD5;
    uint32_t checked, unavailable, mismatches;
    int32_t status = libmpq__archive_verify_ex(
        archive, requested, &checked, &unavailable, &mismatches
    );
    if (status == 0)
        *matched = checked == requested && unavailable == 0 && mismatches == 0;
    return status;
}
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero means requested comparisons completed, possibly with unavailable checks
or mismatches. LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST indicates invalid required pointers;
LIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED rejects writer handles; LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT
rejects unknown flags or malformed required geometry. Existing source read,
seek and size errors propagate. The archive remains caller-owned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_verify (3),
.BR libmpq__file_verify_ex (3)
